Answer: Use the variable name. Example:

```java
int age = 21;
System.out.println(age);
```

Output: 21 The variable name refers to the memory location containing the value.

Answer: Reassignment means giving a new value to a variable that already contains a value. Example:

```java
int age = 21;
age = 30;
```

Here:

```java
age = 30;
```

reassigns the variable.
